Work directly in the hiyroscript/seren repository on the current main implementation.

Implement a focused shield-system visual and behavior update. Preserve the existing architecture, game feel, six-half durability model, wreck/respawn lifecycle, split-screen behavior, car-specific ultimate mechanics, accessibility, and dependency-free Canvas/DOM design.

Do not redesign unrelated HUD systems, hazards, ultimates, collisions, or car mechanics.

Goal

Make four coordinated changes:

1. Change shield depletion order so damage begins with the third/cyan bar instead of the first/pink bar.
2. Restyle all shield bars to remove outlines and half-divider lines and give the colored fill a polished gradient.
3. When a non-view-owner racer survives a hazard collision, briefly show its current shield bar/color and half-state directly above the car for exactly about one second.
4. While a racer’s ultimate is actively running, ordinary shield-consuming hazard contact must not consume a shield half.

These changes must work identically for player one, bots, and local multiplayer racers.

