5. Trigger the above-car indicator on the correct contacts

The temporary shield display should correspond to a real non-destructive hazard contact.

The ordinary durability path can start it through hitShield().

Also account for existing ultimate-specific solid-hazard contact paths that bypass hitShield() entirely because the hazard is smashed.

For example, an ulting car using clearsSolidHazards(who) can physically meet a tumbleweed without shield damage.

That is still a hazard contact and may refresh the temporary shield display, showing the shield state unchanged.

Likewise, if a protected solid meteor is physically struck and smashed by an applicable existing ultimate path without destroying the racer, it can count as surviving hazard contact feedback.

However:

* do not flash on a perfect dodge
* do not flash because a hazard merely passes nearby
* do not flash for a hazard removed elsewhere before reaching the racer
* do not flash for no-contact states
* do not flash for a destroyed racer

Centralize this as much as practical so every hazard does not invent its own timer behavior.

